a52sxq: pinctrl-msm: msm_gpio_mpm_wake_set must not read INTR_CFG without a wakeup-present bit

yupik has no intr_wakeup_present_bit (0 = INTR_ENABLE). msm_gpio_mpm_wake_set() read the GPIO's own
INTR_CFG anyway; with patch 0014 that read hits the TZ-owned GPIOs 48, 51, 56, 59 (qcom,gpios-reserved,
also on wakeup-disabled-gpios) at pinctrl probe and the SoC resets silently (rehearsal rh612p2a45,
2026-11-18). 5.4 only touched the shared wake_reg. Read INTR_CFG only when the SoC has the bit.
(found 2026-11-19; needed by 0014)

--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-msm.c	2026-11-19 07:24:55.304213277 +0200
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-msm.c	2026-11-19 07:24:55.305010905 +0200
@@ -2098,16 +2098,25 @@
 
 	raw_spin_lock_irqsave(&msm_pinctrl_data->lock, flags);
 
-	intr_cfg = msm_readl_intr_cfg(msm_pinctrl_data, g);
-	if (intr_cfg & BIT(g->intr_wakeup_present_bit)) {
-		if (enable)
-			intr_cfg |= BIT(g->intr_wakeup_enable_bit);
-		else
-			intr_cfg &= ~BIT(g->intr_wakeup_enable_bit);
+	/*
+	 * a52sxq: only SoCs with a wakeup-present bit keep the wake enable in the GPIO's own
+	 * INTR_CFG. Without one (yupik: bit 0 = INTR_ENABLE) the test below read the per-GPIO
+	 * register for nothing: on a TZ-owned GPIO (qcom,gpios-reserved 48-51, 56-59, four of
+	 * them on Samsung's wakeup-disabled-gpios list) that read resets the SoC, and on an
+	 * enabled GPIO it cleared INTR_ENABLE instead of the wake bit. 5.4 touched wake_reg only.
+	 */
+	if (g->intr_wakeup_present_bit) {
+		intr_cfg = msm_readl_intr_cfg(msm_pinctrl_data, g);
+		if (intr_cfg & BIT(g->intr_wakeup_present_bit)) {
+			if (enable)
+				intr_cfg |= BIT(g->intr_wakeup_enable_bit);
+			else
+				intr_cfg &= ~BIT(g->intr_wakeup_enable_bit);
 
-		msm_writel_intr_cfg(intr_cfg, msm_pinctrl_data, g);
+			msm_writel_intr_cfg(intr_cfg, msm_pinctrl_data, g);
 
-		goto exit;
+			goto exit;
+		}
 	}
 
 	val = readl_relaxed(msm_pinctrl_data->regs[g->tile] + g->wake_reg);
